#  623cc98 Merge s80-ownpasses: owned passes (Session 80, OWN_RENDERER_PLAN.md "The shadows") - gpu_native_own_steps also lists vertex shaders (v<hash>); a pass of listed draws after the clears of its truth pass (depth and stencil kept when the clears wrote them whole; 8-bit and 16-bit surfaces) goes into an image of ours, resumed when something ends its render pass, going on after a copy (the wrestler maps' blurs join map B's pass); a loss replays every draw. At its copy the clears' pass is turned off (only its clear draws when it loaded tiles); the truth images' tiles it would have written are dirty and our pixels are copied in before any read (draws that are not whole clears, alias loads, stores, copies, write-outs), a whole clear or another image taking them ends that. Copies: whole ones served from our image (or a snapshot when the pass goes on, or with the half-pixel offset gap filled as the game's copy fills it at a resolution scale), 16-bit pages as images of the texture's format filled by the truth texture fill (the copy converts -32..32 to unorm), rectangles into our page images or the game's copy after our pixels are copied in (replayed first for a pass only our image holds); owned pages give unsigned and signed views, unservable bindings are refused; losses pause a shader for 600 frames. At a resolution scale (1440p) owned pages are served at all now: the view check takes the texture's scaled flag, as the shader's constant does (the binding's key never has it - since step 84 every sampler of an owned page was refused there, that frame reading a stale texture), and a left-out copy marks its range scaled as the game's copy does (TextureCache::MarkRangeScaledResolved). PC, the whole shadow chain owned (ring mask + chain, props map, wrestler maps A / B and their blurs): 720p shots byte-identical to owned steps off (5685 vs 5631), every output forced through the replay identical (5660), every dirty tile copied back at once identical (5661), validation 0 (5658); 1440p byte-identical (5690 vs 5664; quick match 5689 vs 5675), forced replay / copy-back identical (5691, 5693), validation 0 (5692), no refused samplers; four Opus reviews' fixes in

